    description: "hypergumbo-lang-scip-python (added 2026-09-19, ea22d7023c) is missing from package lists OUTSIDE the release path. PR #1213 fixed the release-path lists (bump-version, release-check, cov-paths.sh, release.yml build loop, prepare-release) and pinned them with tests/test_release_package_lists.py, which enumerates packages/*/pyproject.toml.\n\nStill missing it (measured by grepping each file for rust-analyzer vs scip-python mentions, 2026-09-25):\n- Scheduled CI installs: .woodpecker/full-suite.yml:94 and .woodpecker/nightly.yml install every lang package EXCEPT scip-python, yet run packages/*/tests/. The scheduled suite is green, so either its scip-python tests error-skip somehow or they import from a path not visible in the install line -- NOT CHECKED. Verify whether scip-python's tests actually execute in the scheduled suite before assuming they do.\n- GitHub-side workflows (ci.yml, full-suite.yml, nightly.yml): same omission; whether those workflows still run is not checked.\n- Lint scanners whose package lists name rust-analyzer but not scip-python: scripts/check-id-construction:40, scripts/check-pass-id-agreement:44, scripts/check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration:66, scripts/check-docstring-drift:136. Each silently skips scip-python's source.\n\nStructural: every one of these is a hand-maintained copy of the package set. Extend the enumeration test to them (or have them read packages/*/pyproject.toml) so the next new package is caught the day it lands."  # f5c1
    fields: {}  # f5c1
